.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt DISPLAY-EXTEND 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm display-extend
.Nd extend the laptop panel to external outputs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Fl Fl right
.Op Fl Fl quiet
.Nm Fl Fl left
.Op Fl Fl quiet
.Nm Fl Fl above
.Op Fl Fl quiet
.Nm Fl Fl off
.Nm Fl Fl toggle
.Op Fl Fl quiet
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
places every connected external RandR output beside the internal
panel.
.Fl Fl right
puts them to the right, each further right than the last.
.Fl Fl left
puts them to the left and the panel to their right.
.Fl Fl above
puts them above the panel.
One of those three,
.Fl Fl off ,
or
.Fl Fl toggle
is required.
.Pp
.Fl Fl off
runs
.Xr display-laptop-only 1 .
.Fl Fl toggle
extends to the right, or runs
.Xr display-laptop-only 1
when the panel is already extended.
.Fl Fl quiet
is passed on in that case.
.Pp
With no external output connected, the extend-none glyph is shown
and the layout is left alone.
.Fl Fl quiet
skips the glyph.
The glyph is
.Xr bosd 1
.Cm mirror-extend
while extending, and
.Cm mirror-extend-none
when there is nothing to extend to.
.Pp
The shared RandR helpers are
.Pa @PREFIX@/libexec/bhotkeys/display-randr-common.subr .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the layout is applied or when no external output is
connected.
It exits 1 when
.Xr xrandr 1
fails or no internal output is found.
A bad argument exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr display-laptop-only 1 ,
.Xr xrandr 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
